{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>See that YHWH, etc.</b> I have explained above that Moses intended to tell them that this commandment does not need to be stated by him to them — rather, behold, they see it themselves, for YHWH gives the commandment directly from Himself to them without any intermediary, as I explained in connection with the verse (Exodus 16:22) ״וַיַּגִּידוּ״ etc. And this is for the greatness of Shabbat, that Israel would see the matter with the faculty of sight. And His saying <b>let no man go out</b> means that YHWH did not bring down the manna on this side, so that they would not need any man to go out from his place, etc. And see what I have written in connection with the verse (Exodus 16:28) ״עַד אָנָה מֵאַנְתֶּם״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:29:01.072161049Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}